// Code that runs once, and code that runs again.
//
// A process runs some of its code once per incarnation and some of it
// again and again. What its once code asks for — a registration made
// from init/1, a monitor its start takes — it asks for once; what code
// that runs again asks for, it asks for again each time. Three questions
// turn on which (docs/design/runs.md):
//
// - coupling (clientlib/restart_state.dl): a request a process's once
//   code makes of a sibling is lost when the sibling restarts, since
//   nothing makes it again;
// - mailbox's monitors (docs/design/monitor-leaks.md): a monitor that
//   code which runs again takes is taken again;
// - mailbox's timer loops and subscriptions: a second arm, or a second
//   subscription, from code that runs again.
//
// The split is per clause where a callback tells its messages apart. A
// clause runs once per incarnation when every message that can enter it
// is made by its process's once code: a start callback (start_callback,
// callbacks.dl: init/1, a Channel's join/3, a LiveView's mount/3), or a
// clause that runs once in turn. That is a positive definition built
// from the message's producers (below); a producer that is unknown,
// repeats, belongs to another process or to code that runs again makes
// the clause code that runs again, the loud direction. "Once" is caused
// by the start alone, bounded per incarnation: an init/1 that sends
// itself one message per item makes that many, and a :DOWN clause for
// the monitors init/1 takes runs once per monitor.
//
// Provides:
//   once_code(mod, func): func may run in mod's once phase: from a start
//     callback, a clause that runs once, the start's continue chain
//     (start_clause: a handle_continue/2 clause init/1's continue enters,
//     whatever else continues to it), or a gated once site, on its own
//     stack: the same process, and no side path (side_call, calls.dl).
//     Seeded at the modules a supervisor starts: coupling's question is
//     about children.
//   once_step(mod, func, site, callee): a call mod's once phase makes at
//     its own level, in a start callback or at a site of the phase, into
//     callee. once_code is the start callbacks and what the steps reach.
//   again_code(func): func runs again and again in the process that runs
//     it: reached, on that process's stack, from a root that runs again
//     as a whole (again_root) or from a call in a clause that runs again.
//     A clause function (below) is again code as a function; a site of
//     one asks once_clause_site.
//   once_clause(func, tag): the clause of the clause function func for
//     tag runs once per incarnation.
//   once_clause_site(site, func): every clause of func the site is in
//     runs once.
//   gated_once_site(site, func): a GenServer handler's site a gate on a
//     field of the state lets run once, whose own run closes the gate
//     and which nothing opens again (below).
//   once_site(site, func): the site runs at most once per incarnation:
//     in a clause that runs once, or gated once.
//   again_root(func, how): where code that runs again as a whole starts:
//     "callback" (runs_again_callback, callbacks.dl, handle_continue/2,
//     a GenEvent handler's handle_event/2 and handle_call/2), "state" (a
//     gen_statem's state function or handle_event/4), "loop" (a receive
//     loop) or "api" (an export only callers outside the program call).
//   A function both kinds reach is both: a helper init/1 and a handler
//   share runs again.
//
// Direction. Loud where the caller is not in view: an export nothing in
// the program calls is taken as called again, though its callers
// outside may call it once. Quiet where the program does not show a
// clause runs once: a message another process sends once, to a process
// it has just started (a channel's join), runs again as far as this
// reads, and so does a site a status field lets run once unless the
// module's returns show the field cannot let it run again.
//
// Requires imports.dl (reach.dl, ways_in.dl, generated.dl, receive.dl)
// and otp.dl (callbacks.dl, calls.dl, supervision.dl, runs_elsewhere.dl).

// ── Clause functions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// clause_callback(mod, func, kind): a callback whose clauses a message
// enters by the tag its first argument's head tells apart (clause_call):
// handle_info/2 ("info") and handle_cast/2 ("cast") by the message,
// handle_continue/2 ("continue") by the continue term, a LiveView's
// handle_async/3 ("async") by the task's name, and a gen_statem's state
// function or handle_event/4 ("internal") by the event type, of which
// only :internal is asked: its other clauses take events from outside.
.decl clause_callback(mod: symbol, func: symbol, kind: symbol)

clause_callback(m, h, "info") :-
  otp_callback(h, m, "handle_info", _),
  function_def(h, m, "handle_info", 2, _).

clause_callback(m, h, "cast") :-
  otp_callback(h, m, "handle_cast", _),
  function_def(h, m, "handle_cast", 2, _).

clause_callback(m, h, "continue") :-
  otp_callback(h, m, "handle_continue", _),
  function_def(h, m, "handle_continue", 2, _).

clause_callback(m, h, "async") :-
  otp_callback(h, m, "handle_async", _),
  function_def(h, m, "handle_async", 3, _).

clause_callback(m, h, "internal") :- statem_event_clause(m, h, _).

// clause_fn(mod, func, kind): func takes, by its clauses, a message mod's
// process is sent: a clause callback of mod, or a function one hands its
// message to whole (hands_on), which takes it where the callback would.
.decl clause_fn(mod: symbol, func: symbol, kind: symbol)

clause_fn(m, h, k) :- clause_callback(m, h, k).
clause_fn(m, g, k) :- hands_on(m, _, g, _, k).

// hands_on(mod, func, callee, site, kind): the call at site hands the
// message func took to callee, whole, as its first argument, and callee
// is the same callback by name and arity (firezone's channels'
// `defdelegate handle_info(msg, s), to: Shared`).
.decl hands_on(mod: symbol, func: symbol, callee: symbol, site: symbol, kind: symbol)

hands_on(m, h, g, c, k) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, k),
  call_instr(h, g, c),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  call_arg_forward(h, g, 0, 0),
  function_def(h, _, n, a, _),
  function_def(g, _, n, a, _).

// A clause of a clause function, by its tag, in mod's process: one some
// call, return or inserted event of the function is told to be in.
.decl clause_node(mod: symbol, func: symbol, kind: symbol, tag: symbol)

clause_node(m, h, k, t) :- clause_fn(m, h, k), k != "internal", message_site_clause(_, h, t).

clause_node(m, h, "internal", ":internal") :-
  clause_fn(m, h, "internal"),
  message_site_clause(_, h, ":internal").

.decl node_tag(kind: symbol, tag: symbol)

node_tag(k, t) :- clause_node(_, _, k, t).

// The clause an instruction of a clause function is in: a call's
// (clause_call), a return's (continue_return, timeout_return), an
// inserted event's (statem_insert).
.decl message_site_clause(site: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

message_site_clause(s, h, t) :- clause_call(s, h, t).
message_site_clause(s, h, t) :- continue_return(s, h, t, _), t != "*".
message_site_clause(s, h, t) :- timeout_return(s, h, t), t != "*".
message_site_clause(s, h, t) :- statem_insert(s, h, t, _), t != "*".

// ── What makes a process a message of its own ────────────────────────
//
// self_message(site, func, kind, tag): the instruction at site, in func,
// makes the process running func a message of kind tagged tag ("*": any
// tag). The producer is where it runs: the rules below attribute it to
// the start callbacks, clauses and roots that reach func on the
// process's stack.
.decl self_message(site: symbol, func: symbol, kind: symbol, tag: symbol)

// A send to self(): the atom, or the tuple tagged by it.
self_message(id, f, "info", t) :-
  pid_send(id, f, msg, "self", _),
  node_tag("info", t),
  (msg = t ; msg = cat("{", cat(t, ", …}"))).

self_message(id, f, "info", "*") :- pid_send(id, f, "dynamic", "self", _).

// A one-shot timer armed for the process (an interval is below).
self_message(id, f, "info", t) :-
  timer_arm(id, f, "self", _, _, _),
  !interval_arm(id),
  timer_tag(id, t, _).

self_message(id, f, "info", "*") :-
  timer_arm(id, f, "self", m, _, _),
  !interval_arm(id),
  m != "param",
  !timer_tag(id, _, _).

self_message(id, f, "info", ":timeout") :- start_timer_arm(id, f, "self").

// A timer armed with a parameter: its message is what the callers hand
// the arming function (a literal atom, a tuple they build with a literal
// tag), at their call. A caller that forwards its own parameter arms it
// in turn.
.decl self_arms_param(func: symbol, pos: number)

self_arms_param(f, k) :- timer_arm(_, f, "self", "param", k, _).
self_arms_param(f, j) :- self_arms_param(g, k), call_arg_forward(f, g, k, j).

self_message(c, f, "info", t) :-
  self_arms_param(g, k),
  call_instr(f, g, c),
  call_arg(f, g, k, t),
  t != "dynamic".

self_message(c, f, "info", t) :-
  self_arms_param(g, k),
  call_instr(f, g, c),
  call_arg_tuple(f, g, k, 0, "literal", t).

self_message(c, f, "info", "*") :-
  self_arms_param(g, k),
  call_instr(f, g, c),
  call_arg(f, g, k, "dynamic"),
  !call_arg_tuple(f, g, k, 0, "literal", _).

self_message(c, f, "info", "*") :-
  self_arms_param(g, k),
  call_instr(f, g, c),
  !call_arg(f, g, k, _),
  !call_arg_forward(f, g, k, _).

// A monitor's :DOWN, and that of a task the process starts and does not
// await (Task.async unawaited, Task.Supervisor.async_nolink).
self_message(id, f, "info", ":DOWN") :- monitor_call(id, f, _).
self_message(id, f, "info", ":DOWN") :- mailbox_writer(id, f, "task").
self_message(id, f, "info", ":DOWN") :- mailbox_writer(id, f, "task_nolink").

// The idle timeout a callback's return arms (`{:noreply, state, ms}`):
// in the callback, or in a function whose result it returns. A helper's
// own `{:ok, a, b}` is no callback's return.
self_message(id, f, "info", ":timeout") :- timeout_return(id, f, _), callback_result(f).

.decl callback_result(func: symbol)

callback_result(f) :- otp_callback(f, _, _, _).
callback_result(g) :- callback_result(f), returns_call(f, g).

// A cast to self().
self_message(id, f, "cast", t) :-
  pid_call(id, f, "cast", "self", _),
  call_tag(id, f, "cast", t).

self_message(id, f, "cast", "*") :-
  pid_call(id, f, "cast", "self", _),
  !call_tag(id, f, "cast", _).

// A return that continues to handle_continue/2.
self_message(id, f, "continue", t) :- continue_return(id, f, _, t).

// An event a gen_statem inserts: :internal, or any type where the
// function does not spell it (ra's `{next_event, EvtType, Evt}`).
self_message(id, f, "internal", ":internal") :-
  statem_insert(id, f, _, t),
  (t = ":internal" ; t = "*").

// A LiveView's start_async/3,4 (Phoenix.LiveView.Async's, under the
// macro): its result enters handle_async/3's clause for the name, in the
// LiveView's process. The call's site is not in the facts, so a start in
// a clause function counts for its every clause (the function stands
// for the site).
self_message(f, f, "async", t) :-
  call_arg(f, g, 1, t),
  t != "dynamic",
  match("Phoenix.(LiveView|LiveComponent)(.Async)?:start_async/[34]", g).

self_message(f, f, "async", "*") :-
  call_arg(f, g, 1, "dynamic"),
  match("Phoenix.(LiveView|LiveComponent)(.Async)?:start_async/[34]", g).

// A call of a clause function of the caller's own module, other than a
// hand-on: its first argument is the message, and the clause it enters
// runs in the caller's process.
self_message(c, f, k, t) :-
  clause_fn(_, h, k),
  call_instr(f, h, c),
  !hands_on(_, f, h, c, _),
  function_def(f, fm, _, _, _),
  function_def(h, fm, _, _, _),
  (call_arg(f, h, 0, t) ; call_arg_tuple(f, h, 0, 0, "literal", t)),
  t != "dynamic".

self_message(c, f, k, "*") :-
  clause_fn(_, h, k),
  call_instr(f, h, c),
  !hands_on(_, f, h, c, _),
  function_def(f, fm, _, _, _),
  function_def(h, fm, _, _, _),
  !call_arg_tuple(f, h, 0, 0, "literal", _),
  (call_arg(f, h, 0, "dynamic") ; !call_arg(f, h, 0, _)).

// ── What another process may make ────────────────────────────────────
//
// outside_message(kind, tag): a message some process other than the
// receiver's own code may make: a send or a one-shot timer to a process
// other than the sender's, a cast that is not to self(), an interval to
// another process, and what Phoenix.PubSub delivers.
.decl outside_message(kind: symbol, tag: symbol)

outside_message("info", t) :-
  pid_send(_, _, msg, src, _),
  src != "self",
  node_tag("info", t),
  (msg = t ; msg = cat("{", cat(t, ", …}"))).

outside_message("info", t) :- timer_arm(id, _, "other", _, _, _), timer_tag(id, t, _).

outside_message("cast", t) :-
  call_tag(id, f, "cast", t),
  !pid_call(id, f, "cast", "self", _).

// An interval timer (`:timer.send_interval/2,3`) sends its message again
// and again, wherever it is armed: one armed for another process is that
// process's again and again, and one a process arms for itself is code
// that runs again in it (repeated_message).
.decl interval_arm(site: symbol)

interval_arm(id) :- timer_arm(id, f, _, _, _, _), arms_interval(f).

// A function that calls :timer.send_interval/2,3: its timer arms are
// all taken as the interval's (a one-shot beside it repeats as far as
// this reads, the loud direction).
.decl arms_interval(func: symbol)

arms_interval(f) :- call_arg(f, g, _, _), match(":timer:send_interval/[23]", g).

outside_message("info", t) :-
  interval_arm(id),
  timer_arm(id, _, "other", _, _, _),
  timer_tag(id, t, _),
  node_tag("info", t).

.decl repeated_message(site: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

repeated_message(id, f, t) :-
  interval_arm(id),
  timer_arm(id, f, "self", _, _, _),
  timer_tag(id, t, _).

repeated_message(id, f, "*") :-
  interval_arm(id),
  timer_arm(id, f, "self", _, _, _),
  !timer_tag(id, _, _).

// What Phoenix.PubSub delivers: a message the program hands its
// broadcast (`Phoenix.PubSub.broadcast(ps, topic, {:refresh, x})`),
// itself or through a function of its own that hands a parameter on to
// one. The library sends it from its own code, which the program's
// facts do not show, to every subscriber.
.decl publishes_param(func: symbol, pos: number)

publishes_param(f, k) :-
  call_arg_forward(f, g, _, k),
  match("Phoenix.PubSub:(local_|direct_)?broadcast(_from)?!?/[3-5]", g).

publishes_param(f, k) :- publishes_param(g, gk), call_arg_forward(f, g, gk, k).

.decl published(tag: symbol)

published(t) :-
  (call_arg(_, g, _, t) ; call_arg_tuple(_, g, _, 0, "literal", t)),
  match("Phoenix.PubSub:(local_|direct_)?broadcast(_from)?!?/[3-5]", g).

published(t) :-
  publishes_param(f, k),
  (call_arg(_, f, k, t) ; call_arg_tuple(_, f, k, 0, "literal", t)).

outside_message("info", t) :- published(t), node_tag("info", t).

// A call of a clause function from another module, other than a
// hand-on: its clauses run in whatever process that caller runs in.
.decl called_from_outside(func: symbol)

called_from_outside(h) :-
  clause_fn(_, h, _),
  call_instr(f, h, c),
  !hands_on(_, f, h, c, _),
  function_def(f, fm, _, _, _),
  function_def(h, hm, _, _, _),
  fm != hm.

// ── Where each producer runs ─────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The functions that reach a producer on their own stack.
.init message_reach = SameProcessReach

message_reach.seed(p, p) :- self_message(_, p, _, _).
message_reach.seed(p, p) :- repeated_message(_, p, _).

// produced(from, part, mod, kind, tag): what runs at `from` makes mod's
// process a message of kind tagged tag. `from` is a clause function of
// mod with `part` its clause ("*" for sites no clause tag names: every
// clause reaches them, a catch-all among them), "start" (mod's start
// callbacks), or "again" (a root that runs again as a whole, of mod, or
// "*" where the process is not known).
.decl produced(from: symbol, part: symbol, mod: symbol, kind: symbol, tag: symbol)

produced(h, t, m, k, tag) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  self_message(s, h, k, tag),
  message_site_clause(s, h, t).

produced(h, "*", m, k, tag) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  self_message(s, h, k, tag),
  !message_site_clause(s, h, _).

produced(h, t, m, k, tag) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  call_instr(h, g, c),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !hands_on(m, h, g, c, _),
  clause_call(c, h, t),
  message_reach.reaches(g, p),
  self_message(_, p, k, tag).

produced(h, "*", m, k, tag) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  call_instr(h, g, c),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !hands_on(m, h, g, c, _),
  !clause_call(c, h, _),
  message_reach.reaches(g, p),
  self_message(_, p, k, tag).

produced(h, t, m, k, tag) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  fun_handed(c, h, g, _),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  clause_call(c, h, t),
  message_reach.reaches(g, p),
  self_message(_, p, k, tag).

produced(h, "*", m, k, tag) :-
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  call_edge(h, g),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !call_instr(h, g, _),
  message_reach.reaches(g, p),
  self_message(_, p, k, tag).

produced("start", m, m, k, tag) :-
  start_callback(m, s),
  message_reach.reaches(s, p),
  self_message(_, p, k, tag).

produced("again", m, m, k, tag) :-
  again_whole(r, m),
  message_reach.reaches(r, p),
  self_message(_, p, k, tag).

// An interval timer's message, in the process whose code arms it.
produced("again", m, m, "info", tag) :- runs_in(m, p), repeated_message(_, p, tag).

.decl runs_in(mod: symbol, func: symbol)

runs_in(m, p) :- start_callback(m, s), message_reach.reaches(s, p).
runs_in(m, p) :- clause_fn(m, h, _), message_reach.reaches(h, p).
runs_in(m, p) :- again_whole(r, m), message_reach.reaches(r, p).

// A producer no root the program knows reaches (a fun made to run
// elsewhere or later): its process is not known.
.decl rooted(func: symbol)

rooted(p) :- start_callback(_, s), message_reach.reaches(s, p).
rooted(p) :- clause_fn(_, h, _), message_reach.reaches(h, p).
rooted(p) :- again_whole(r, _), message_reach.reaches(r, p).

produced("again", "*", "*", k, tag) :- self_message(_, p, k, tag), !rooted(p).

// The roots of code that runs again as a whole: a callback no clause of
// which is told apart (handle_call/3, a channel's handle_in/3), a
// receive loop and an export only callers outside call. `mod` is the
// process's module, "*" where the process is not known.
.decl again_whole(func: symbol, mod: symbol)

again_whole(e, m) :-
  (again_root(e, "callback") ; again_root(e, "state")),
  function_def(e, m, _, _, _),
  !clause_fn(_, e, _).

again_whole(e, "*") :- again_root(e, "loop").
again_whole(e, "*") :- again_root(e, "api").

// An export only callers outside call may be a callback of a behaviour
// the module declares that no table here lists (a LiveComponent's
// update/2): its library runs it where it runs the module's other
// callbacks. Its own module's clauses count it, whatever the stack.
again_whole(e, m) :- again_root(e, "api"), function_def(e, m, _, _, _).

// Code no process of the program runs on its own stack — an export only
// callers outside call, a receive loop, a fun made to run elsewhere —
// runs on a process's stack only through a call the call graph does not
// follow: an apply of a module or function it does not know, a fun
// value's call, a protocol's dispatch. A process whose code makes none
// runs only what the graph shows.
.decl opaque_call(func: symbol)

opaque_call(f) :- dynamic_call(id, f, _), !resolved_apply(id, f, _).
opaque_call(f) :- protocol_dispatch(_, f, _).

.init opaque_reach = SameProcessReachSet

opaque_reach.seed(f) :- opaque_call(f).

.decl opaque_stack(mod: symbol)

opaque_stack(m) :- start_callback(m, s), opaque_reach.reaches(s).
opaque_stack(m) :- clause_fn(m, h, _), opaque_reach.reaches(h).
opaque_stack(m) :- again_whole(r, m), opaque_reach.reaches(r).

// ── Once clauses ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// enters(from, part, mod, func, tag): what runs at (from, part) makes a
// message clause (func, tag) takes in mod's process.
.decl enters(from: symbol, part: symbol, mod: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

enters(a, b, m, h, t) :- clause_node(m, h, k, t), produced(a, b, m, k, t).
enters(a, b, m, h, t) :- clause_node(m, h, k, t), produced(a, b, m, k, "*").

enters("again", "*", m, h, t) :-
  clause_node(m, h, k, t),
  (produced("again", "*", "*", k, t) ; produced("again", "*", "*", k, "*")),
  opaque_stack(m).

// Some producer spells the clause's tag. A message only a producer of
// any tag may carry may come from the runtime or a library under that
// tag, which the program's facts do not show.
.decl entered(mod: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

entered(m, h, t) :- clause_node(m, h, k, t), produced(_, _, m, k, t).

// A clause that runs again in mod's process: another process may make
// what it takes, or code that runs again, a part of a clause function
// that does (again_part), or the clause itself round a cycle of
// producers — init/1 arms `:tick`, and the `:tick` clause arms it again.
// A least fixpoint of positive rules: a clause is not assumed to run
// once to show it runs once.
.decl runs_again(mod: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

runs_again(m, h, t) :- clause_node(m, h, k, t), outside_message(k, t).
runs_again(m, h, t) :- clause_node(m, h, _, t), called_from_outside(h).
runs_again(m, h, t) :- enters("again", _, m, h, t).
runs_again(m, h, t) :- enters(a, b, m, h, t), again_part(m, a, b).
runs_again(m, h, t) :- enters_path(h, t, m, h, t).

// A part of a clause function that runs again: its untold sites, a
// clause whose producers are not asked (a gen_statem's clause for an
// event from outside), one no producer spells the tag of, one that runs
// again.
.decl again_part(mod: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

again_part(m, h, "*") :- clause_fn(m, h, _).

again_part(m, h, t) :-
  produced(h, t, m, _, _),
  clause_fn(m, h, _),
  !clause_node(m, h, _, t).

again_part(m, h, t) :- clause_node(m, h, _, t), !entered(m, h, t).
again_part(m, h, t) :- runs_again(m, h, t).

// The clauses a clause's producers lead to, through the clauses between.
.decl enters_path(from: symbol, part: symbol, mod: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

enters_path(a, b, m, h, t) :- enters(a, b, m, h, t), clause_fn(m, a, _).
enters_path(a, b, m, h, t) :- enters_path(a, b, m, g, u), enters(g, u, m, h, t).

.decl runs_again_somewhere(func: symbol, tag: symbol)

runs_again_somewhere(h, t) :- runs_again(_, h, t).

// once_clause(func, tag): some producer spells what the clause takes, and
// in every process that runs func nothing makes it run again.
.decl once_clause(func: symbol, tag: symbol)

once_clause(h, t) :-
  entered(m, h, t),
  clause_node(m, h, _, t),
  !runs_again_somewhere(h, t).

// A site of a clause function every clause of which it is in runs once.
.decl once_clause_site(site: symbol, func: symbol)

once_clause_site(s, h) :-
  once_clause(h, t),
  clause_call(s, h, t),
  !again_tag_site(s, h).

.decl again_tag_site(site: symbol, func: symbol)

again_tag_site(s, h) :- clause_fn(_, h, _), clause_call(s, h, t), !once_clause(h, t).

// ── Once by the state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A GenServer handler that asks its state whether it has done a thing
// yet, does it, and records that it has: `handle_info(:registered,
// %{registered: false} = s)` arms its loop and returns `%{s | registered:
// true}`. Whatever enters the clause again finds the field set, and the
// arm does not run. A site runs at most once per incarnation this way
// when all of these hold:
//
// - every path to it passes a test of a field of the state that admits
//   only some atoms (state_gate, Argus.Extractors.StateGate): `false`,
//   `nil`, `:awaiting_boot`;
// - every way the handler completes after it hands back that field
//   outside them, or ends the process (gate_closed): `true`, a pid, a
//   ref, `:booted`;
// - no return of the module's handlers or code_change/3 sets the field
//   to an atom the gate admits, or to a value the return does not show
//   (state_return). init/1 starts the field there for each incarnation,
//   and terminate/2's return is dropped;
// - nothing in the program calls the handler: the state it is handed is
//   the process's own, and what it returns is what the process keeps.
//   A call of a handler with a state of the caller's making runs the
//   site whatever the process holds.
//
// A GenServer's state_setter callbacks (callbacks.dl) set its state:
// a result of a shape GenServer does not return reads as any state.

// Some return of the module sets the gated field to what the gate at
// site admits, or to a value it does not show: the gate may open again.
.decl gate_reopened(site: symbol, func: symbol, key: symbol)

gate_reopened(s, f, k) :-
  state_gate(s, f, k, v),
  function_def(f, m, _, _, _),
  state_setter(m, c),
  (state_return(c, _, k, v) ; state_return(c, _, k, "dynamic")).

.decl gated_once_site(site: symbol, func: symbol)

gated_once_site(s, f) :-
  state_gate(s, f, k, _),
  gate_closed(s, f, k),
  function_def(f, m, _, _, _),
  state_setter(m, f),
  !call_edge(_, f),
  !gate_reopened(s, f, k).

// A site that runs at most once per incarnation: in a clause that runs
// once, or behind a gate its run closes.
.decl once_site(site: symbol, func: symbol)

once_site(s, f) :- once_clause_site(s, f).
once_site(s, f) :- gated_once_site(s, f).

// A handler's callee every call of which is at a gated site: the reach
// from the handler, which runs again as a whole, does not follow it.
.decl gated_edge(func: symbol, callee: symbol)

gated_edge(f, g) :- gated_once_site(c, f), call_instr(f, g, c), !open_edge(f, g).
gated_edge(f, g) :- gated_once_site(c, f), fun_handed(c, f, g, _), !open_edge(f, g).

.decl open_edge(func: symbol, callee: symbol)

open_edge(f, g) :- gated_once_site(_, f), call_instr(f, g, c), !gated_once_site(c, f).
open_edge(f, g) :- gated_once_site(_, f), fun_handed(c, f, g, _), !gated_once_site(c, f).

open_edge(f, g) :-
  gated_once_site(_, f),
  call_edge(f, g),
  !call_instr(f, g, _),
  !fun_handed(_, f, g, _).

// ── Once code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// once_code is what may run in a process's once phase: its start
// callbacks, the clauses that run once (once_clause), and the start's
// continue chain — a handle_continue/2 clause init/1's continue enters,
// or one a clause of the chain continues to (start_clause). gen_server
// runs init/1's continue before any message, as part of the start,
// whatever else continues to the same clause later: coupling asks what a
// start may ask for once, and a request the start makes there may not be
// made again after its peer's restart (jackalope's Hare, whose
// handle_continue/2 init/1 and every reconnect continue to). A clause a
// message enters is not part of the start unless it runs once: a
// periodic loop init/1 arms asks again on every tick. once_clause is the
// stricter word, for the readers asking what cannot run again.
.decl start_clause(mod: symbol, func: symbol, tag: symbol)

start_clause(m, h, t) :- once_clause(h, t), clause_node(m, h, _, t).

start_clause(m, h, t) :-
  clause_node(m, h, "continue", t),
  enters("start", m, m, h, t).

start_clause(m, h, t) :-
  clause_node(m, h, "continue", t),
  enters(a, b, m, h, t),
  start_clause(m, a, b).

// A site of mod's handler func that runs in mod's once phase: in a
// clause of the phase, or behind a gate on the state its own run closes
// (gated_once_site), whatever enters the handler.
.decl once_phase_site(mod: symbol, func: symbol, site: symbol)

once_phase_site(m, h, s) :- start_clause(m, h, t), clause_call(s, h, t).
once_phase_site(m, h, s) :- gated_once_site(s, h), function_def(h, m, _, _, _).

// The calls mod's once phase makes at its own level: a call its start
// callback makes, or the call at a site of the phase (a
// handle_continue/2 clause init/1 continues to). Everything else once
// code runs is below one of them, and the step is mod's own code where
// what it reaches may be a helper's or another module's API: where a
// finding about a request once code makes points (coupling's
// holds_site).
.decl once_step(mod: symbol, func: symbol, site: symbol, callee: symbol)

once_step(m, s, c, g) :-
  start_callback(m, s),
  child_subtree(_, _, m),
  call_instr(s, g, c),
  !side_call(s, g).

once_step(m, s, c, g) :-
  start_callback(m, s),
  child_subtree(_, _, m),
  fun_handed(c, s, g, _),
  !runs_elsewhere(s, g),
  !side_call(s, g).

once_step(m, h, c, g) :-
  child_subtree(_, _, m),
  once_phase_site(m, h, c),
  call_instr(h, g, c),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !side_call(h, g).

once_step(m, h, c, g) :-
  child_subtree(_, _, m),
  once_phase_site(m, h, c),
  fun_handed(c, h, g, _),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g).

// A start callback's own steps are on its walk already; rooting them
// too keeps once_code what the steps reach.
.init once_reach = ForwardSameProcessReachCut

once_reach.cut(f, g) :- side_call(f, g).
once_reach.root(m, s) :- start_callback(m, s), child_subtree(_, _, m).
once_reach.root(m, g) :- once_step(m, _, _, g).

.decl once_code(mod: symbol, func: symbol)

once_code(m, g) :- once_reach.reaches(m, g).

// ── Code that runs again ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.decl again_root(func: symbol, how: symbol)

again_root(e, "callback") :-
  otp_callback(e, m, n, _),
  function_def(e, m, n, a, _),
  runs_again_callback(n, a).

// handle_continue/2 runs whenever a return continues to it: once from
// init/1, again from a handler. Its clauses are told apart by what
// continues to them (once_clause).
again_root(e, "callback") :- clause_callback(_, e, "continue").

again_root(e, "callback") :-
  otp_callback(e, m, n, "GenEvent"),
  function_def(e, m, n, 2, _),
  (n = "handle_event" ; n = "handle_call").

again_root(f, "state") :- statem_event_clause(_, f, _).

again_root(f, "loop") :-
  receives(f),
  call_edge(f, g),
  !runs_elsewhere(f, g),
  loop_back.reaches(g, f).

// A function only callers outside the program call (api_export,
// ways_in.dl), which may call it on every use: no function of the
// program calls it, it is no process's callback, no start of the program
// runs it (process_start: a process's body, run once per process), no
// supervisor starts it (the start_link of a module a child spec names),
// and no library's macro wrote it (library_written, generated.dl: such a
// function is the library's to call, as HTTPoison calls the transformer
// its `use` writes, once per spawned process).
again_root(f, "api") :-
  api_export(f),
  !call_edge(_, f),
  !process_entry(_, f),
  !library_written(f),
  !child_start(f),
  !process_start(_, _, _, _, f).

// The start_link/N of a module a supervisor starts: its caller is the
// supervisor, through the child spec (the call graph shows no edge), once
// per start of the child.
.decl child_start(func: symbol)

child_start(f) :- child_subtree(_, _, m), function_def(f, m, "start_link", _, _).

// A receive loop's way back to itself, on its own stack.
.init loop_back = SameProcessReach

loop_back.seed(f, f) :- receives(f).

// Reached from a root that runs again as a whole, or from a call of a
// clause function at a site that does not run once (once_site: a clause
// not once, a site no clause tag names, a call no gate closes).
// The reach does not enter a clause function by a call: entering one is
// a message, and its clauses are judged by what enters them.
.init again_reach = ForwardSameProcessReachSetCut

again_reach.cut(f, g) :- side_call(f, g).
again_reach.cut(f, g) :- call_edge(f, g), clause_fn(_, g, _).
again_reach.cut(f, g) :- gated_edge(f, g).
again_reach.root(f) :- again_root(f, _), !clause_fn(_, f, _).

again_reach.root(g) :-
  clause_fn(_, h, _),
  call_instr(h, g, c),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !side_call(h, g),
  !hands_on(_, h, g, c, _),
  !once_site(c, h).

again_reach.root(g) :-
  clause_fn(_, h, _),
  fun_handed(c, h, g, _),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !once_site(c, h).

again_reach.root(g) :-
  clause_fn(_, h, _),
  call_edge(h, g),
  !runs_elsewhere(h, g),
  !side_call(h, g),
  !call_instr(h, g, _),
  !fun_handed(_, h, g, _).

.decl again_code(func: symbol)

again_code(f) :- again_reach.reaches(f).
again_code(h) :- clause_fn(_, h, _).
